From: Hermes Patches <patches@local>
Subject: [PATCH] feat(gateway): /gpmode per-chat group reply mode (mention/free/auto)

Adds a persistent per-chat group reply-mode toggle for Telegram groups/topics,
settable at runtime via the /gpmode slash command:

  /gpmode status | mention | free | auto

  - mention : reply only when addressed (@mention, reply-to-bot, /cmd@bot,
              or configured wake-word patterns). Aliases: strict, mentions, @.
  - free    : reply to every allowed group message. Aliases: always, all, open.
  - auto    : "smart-observe" — mention-dispatch today; reserved for future
              semantic auto-reply classification (NOT yet enabled; honest stub).

State persists to ~/.hermes/gateway_group_modes.json, keyed per
platform:chat[:thread] with chat-level inheritance for topics.

Two correctness fixes over the initial sketch:
  1. The gate referenced a bare `_hermes_home` that only exists in run.py, not
     telegram.py — it raised NameError swallowed by `except`, leaving every
     override permanently INERT. Now uses the module-level `get_hermes_home()`.
  2. `get_group_mode(..., default=None)` so a chat with NO explicit /gpmode
     override falls through to the operator's configured require_mention
     behavior (backward compatible) instead of being forced to mention-only.

DMs are unaffected (always private). Verified: 49 gateway gpmode/gating tests
pass; group_mode store round-trip + thread inheritance + backward-compat default
verified. Live Telegram E2E pending a gateway restart.
